<header><p class="st-kicker">city state · Greece and the Aegean</p><h1 class="st-title">Aenus</h1><p class="st-meta">600 BCE – 146 BCE (approx.) · capital Aenus</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Aeolian city at the mouth of the Hebrus river in Thrace, a gateway for trade with the Thracian interior.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Aenus was founded by Aeolian settlers from <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/mytilene">Mytilene</a> and Cyme on a hill at the mouth of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maritsa">Hebrus</a>, the modern Maritsa or Evros, on the Thracian coast. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/homer">Homer</a> mentions a Thracian named from Aenus, and the city flourished from the 6th century BCE.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Aenus traded salt fish and goods with the Thracian interior along the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maritsa">Hebrus</a>, including the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/odrysian-kingdom">Odrysian Kingdom</a>. It struck fine <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silver">silver</a> coins with the head of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hermes">Hermes</a>. Aenus paid tribute in the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/delian-league">Delian League</a> and fought on the Athenian side at <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/syracuse">Syracuse</a> in 413 BCE.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hellenistic-period">Hellenistic period</a> Aenus was held in turn by the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/ptolemaic-empire">Ptolemaic Empire</a> and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/antigonid-kingdom-of-macedonia">Antigonid Kingdom of Macedonia</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> declared it free in 167 BCE, and it came under Roman control by 146 BCE. It is today the Turkish town of Enez.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="city state, 600 BCE – 146 BCE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M24 82 V42 H32 V34 H40 V42 H46 V34 H54 V42 H60 V34 H68 V42 H76 V82 Z"/><path d="M44 82 V66 Q50 58 56 66 V82"/><path d="M34 54 H40 M60 54